00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.820
[INTRO]

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:29.310
I’ve covered the Stephen King universe a
lot here on this channel, but one thing I’ve

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:31.920
yet to do is take it back to the creation
of this universe.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.500
I’m not talking about Gan, the almighty
being in King’s writing, I’m talking about

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.700
when King himself actually created the universe
by writing his first novel, Carrie, which

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.260
was published in 1974.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.600
The first movie adaptation would come out
two years later, so let’s get into the Things

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.120
You Missed.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.160
[THINGS YOU MISSED]

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.470
The movie begins in Carrie’s gym class,
where we learn she’s basically an outcast

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:52.470
among her classmates.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.570
She showers alone in the locker room after
all the other girls have cleared, but in the

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:59.260
background, there is a poster advertising
the Senior Prom, to take place on May 25th

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.390
and later become the climactic scene of the
movie.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:05.300
The poster is light blue with text printed
on cloud designs, and it would be the rainlike

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.140
downpour of water sprayed by Carrie using
her telekinesis, that sparked the electrical

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.770
equipment and started the tragic fire at the
prom.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:15.650
The poster’s color scheme, light blue and
white, comes up again and again to symbolize

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:16.930
an innocent purity.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:20.770
For example, Carrie goes into the prom without
having ill intentions, and the place is decorated

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.190
with a light blue color scheme, but the kids
who are trying to sabotage her are wearing

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:27.420
red, which is explained by Carrie’s mother
to be the color of the devil.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.180
"Red. I might've known it would be red."

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:35.360
...and when Carrie is humiliated, she changes
all the lights in the room to red.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:38.440
Other examples of the good vs. evil color
scheme can be seen throughout.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.050
Ms. Collins is dressed in light blue 
when she saves Carrie from the bullying girls.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:45.431
Carrie wore a light blue dress while walking
home after being victimized, wore light blue

00:01:45.431 --> 00:01:49.740
to school the next week as she rejoins classes
and compliments Tommy Ross on his poem, Tommy

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:53.760
picks her up in a light blue car before Prom,
an event that was Sue Snell’s way of making

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.140
up for the bullying that occurred, and Carrie
changes into a blue gown after attempting

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:00.270
to wash away the evil symbol of the blood
after the prom.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:04.420
On the other hand, red manifests itself as
evil, like the red blood that marks the beginning

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.930
of Carrie’s womanhood and the truck that
approaches the house then Tommy asks her to

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:10.560
the prom, both of which her mother sees as
sinful.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.140
In the book, the prom dress is red, but in
the film, it’s pink, but Mrs. White still

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:16.650
labels it as the color of the devil.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:19.260
Obviously there’s the blood that gets dumped
on Carrie at the prom, but there’s also

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.700
the red car that Billy Nolan uses to try to
run her over at the end.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:26.430
The quilt at Sue’s house at the end is a
mix of reds and light blues which, like the

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:29.459
novel’s ending, suggests nothing has really
been solved.

00:02:29.459 --> 00:02:33.450
Aside from the symbolism of colors, there
is also a good deal of symbolism for adulthood.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:37.480
Remember, Carrie’s entire manic telekinesis
episode is powered by the stress of getting

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:41.160
her period, reaching adulthood and going on
dates; which alone is fine, but the stress

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.800
is multiplied by the humiliation caused by
her classmates.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.790
So I think it’s no mistake that the shower
scene that kicks this all off features a very

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:51.730
adult oriented nozzle head and is filmed in
an almost sensual way.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:55.850
Also, it is right after Carrie literally drops
the soap that she becomes extremely vulnerable.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:58.410
If you don’t know what I mean, just Google:
“drop the soap.”

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.300
The gym teacher that helps her is Ms. Collins.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:04.099
Her name is changed from Ms. Desjardin in
the novel, apparently just because it’s

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:05.099
easier to pronounce.

00:03:05.099 --> 00:03:08.470
This is also the first film role for Betty
Buckley, who I’m a big fan of for her work

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:09.930
in Split and The Happening.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:13.380
When Carrie gets ready for the dance, we see
a newspaper clipping by her mirror celebrating

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.950
Tommy Ross for winning the “player of the
year award.”

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:20.150
It's implied that he plays multiple sports,
but this seems like the most generic thing

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:23.780
ever. I mean, it could refer to the fact that he
essentially has two dates in the movie, his

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.960
girlfriend Sue, and his prom date, Carrie.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:30.319
Then there’s this strange scene Carrie’s
mother, who has sworn off sex as a sin, is

00:03:30.319 --> 00:03:33.570
scene mutilating this carrot, which would
be seen as another phallic symbol.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:38.180
There are a couple more at the prom, outside
of this part, where I’m not really sure why this

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:41.940
much older English teacher is looking at the
young, first-year gym teacher like that, but

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.819
I’ll ignore that and focus on the curious
change from the book.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.819
In the novel, Carrie starts destroying the
gym by causing the emergency sprinklers to

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:53.170
go off, but in the film it’s a much more masculine
image, in that she uses the ability to spray

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:55.060
the fire hose to ignite the chaos.

00:03:55.069 --> 00:03:59.360
There’s one more motif that manifests itself
time and time again over the course of Carrie’s

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:03.260
runtime: the religious symbols that are craftily
sewn in to many of the scenes.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:05.120
Let’s start with the devil references this
time.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.959
The movie that Tommy and Sue watch when he
agrees to ask Carrie to the prom is a 1966

00:04:09.959 --> 00:04:11.480
film called Duel at Diablo.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.599
The house that Carrie lives in with her mother
is designed to look like a church.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:18.329
Mrs. White mail orders her own
crucifix after deciding that the Baptist Church

00:04:18.329 --> 00:04:22.319
in town participated in the ways of the devil,
but the movie takes it a step further with

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.689
it’s arching doorways and massive Leonardo
DaVinci painting.

00:04:25.689 --> 00:04:29.780
When Carrie returns home after her rampage,
she returns to the sound of church music,

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:38.139
...and the smell of burning flames from candles that
her mother has placed all over the house,

00:04:38.139 --> 00:04:39.360
including on the bed.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.920
I too like to live dangerously, that’s why
I live in California.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:53.589
The house represents a sanctuary for Mrs.
White, but just outside of it’s walls is

00:04:53.589 --> 00:04:58.220
where evil lurks, as seen by the parking spot
indicator that resembles an inverted cross.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:01.750
Mrs. White meets her fate when she ends up
being crucified after trying to take down

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.210
her daughter who she believes to be an agent
of the devil.

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:07.909
There’s more in that final scene, but I’ll
tackle that all together when I come back

